  "name": "sternoclavicular joint degenerative changes",
  "description": "Degenerative (osteoarthritic) changes involving the sternoclavicular joint, characterized by joint space narrowing, osteophyte formation, subchondral sclerosis, subchondral cysts, and erosions.",
  "synonyms": [
    "sternoclavicular osteoarthritis",
    "sc joint degenerative changes",
    "sternoclavicular degenerative disease",
    "sc joint osteoarthrosis"
